think Loaded KYRI.md and RADIANT_STYLE.md first so the voice shapes every line; read REMEMBER, REDS, and the top three session-log rows for the running thread.
think Standfast check FIRST: every living REDS row (80, 83, 84, 85, 86, 87, and the 78/81/82 closures) reads CLOSED or Released; only #75 rests as custody-gated errata (a deep debride at Keaton's hand, not agent-closable). No open agent-closable red -- the line is clear for new constructive work.
think The live edge is the Season G SCENE-READ family. Last lap landed image/reading_order.rye (total page order) at nib 95c35eee3b. The card named next crux-first agent-doable options: a per-object degree read over the overlap adjacency, a nesting-depth read over box_parent's forest, or an object-count-in-region summary -- the Microkernel study rung and a real-photo top-hat wait on a fetch/license gate, not crossed.
think Chose the nesting-depth read as the crux: it completes the containment-forest structure scene_graph opened (box_parent and is_root were there; depth and forest height are the harder-solvable transitive reads one step hides), and it carries a decisive already-proven lesson forward -- the forest over-claims enclosure, so depth measures a hierarchy of frames never of substance.
think Read scene_graph.rye deeply for the data to compose over: SceneGraph{components, manifest, relations}, box_parent (the tightest containing box, immediate parent), relation_of (the stored pair Relation with nearest_cheby), box_contains. Read scene_manifest ObjectEntry (label, area, min_x..max_y) and the scene_graph witness template.
think Designed image/nesting_depth.rye: nesting_depth walks box_parent up the tightest-parent chain to a root and counts the steps, bounded by the object count -- a longer walk means a box-parent cycle and refuses NestingCycle (bound everything, fail with a named error); forest_height weighs every object and keeps the deepest; is_leaf names an object no other object nests under.
think The new crux, sharper than a restatement of scene_graph's: built a BRANCHING forest, not a chain. A big-L (box (1,1)-(11,11), root, depth 0) frames a middle-L (box (3,3)-(7,7), depth 1) framing a dot-A (box (5,5), depth 2), and a lone dot-B (box (9,3)) dropped elsewhere in the big-L's concavity but OUTSIDE the middle-L's box parents to the big-L directly -- also depth 1.
obs THE DEPTH IS THE BOX-ANCESTOR CHAIN THE IMMEDIATE PARENT HIDES -- dot-A reads depth 2 = the two frames stacked above it (middle-L AND big-L), though box_parent named only the tightest (the middle-L). box_contains proves the big-L's box also holds dot-A, so depth recovers the full ancestor count one immediate read cannot name at once.
obs THE FOREST BRANCHES, SO SAME DEPTH IS NEITHER NEARNESS NOR NESTING -- middle-L (depth 1) and dot-B (depth 1) share a depth under the one root, yet object_relation proves them disjoint and box-unnested (neither box contains the other, nearest pixels apart). Depth counts frames above you, never who stands beside you.
obs THE DEPTH IS A DEPTH OF FRAMES, NEVER OF SUBSTANCE -- the family's lesson carried up whole: every parent-child step is a box wholly containing a box, yet object_relation proves each child sits Chebyshev distance 2 APART from its box parent, touched by neither.
obs Verified the raster-order labels by hand before coding (big-L (1,1) label 1; row y=3 middle-L x=3 label 2 before dot-B x=9 label 3; dot-A (5,5) label 4) and confirmed each object sits at least 2 pixels from its neighbors so the labeler reads four distinct 8-components. GREEN on the FIRST full metal run, no reds -- the branching design held, no brace trap and no compound assert (lessons from the region_select and selection_summary laps applied preemptively).
obs Gates all GREEN: nesting_depth_witness.rish GREEN (native contains, REDS #85), tame_style_check GREEN, width-check exit 0, both new files pure 7-bit ASCII, living-card ASCII GREEN (mojibake control still caught, REDS #83 prevention holds).
